<title>SOUTH AFRICA: CRICKET-FREE STATE CRUSH TRANSVAAL.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-FREE STATE CRUSH TRANSVAAL.</headline>
<dateline>BLOEMFONTEIN 1997-01-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transvaal crashed to a</p>
<p>second successive Supersport Series defeat with a day to spare</p>
<p>at the hands of Freed State at Springbok Park on Sunday.</p>
<p>Transvaal, in the hunt for the title after three</p>
<p>back-to-back wins earlier in the seasons, were bowled out for a</p>
<p>meagre 108 in their second innings to follow hard on the heels</p>
<p>of their defeat by Border.</p>
<p>They were dismissed in only 38 overs on a bouncy Springbok</p>
<p>Park wicket with four of the top five contributing only six</p>
<p>between them as Sarel Cilliers and Nico Pretorius exploited the</p>
<p>conditions to the full.</p>
<p>Only opener Mark Benfield (26) provided prolonged resistance</p>
<p>at the top of the order and although Ross Veenstra (26) and</p>
<p>Andrew Hall (25) shared a 30 run partnership for the eighth</p>
<p>wicket the victory target of 301 was never in sight.</p>
<p>Pretorius finished with match figures of seven for 55 as</p>
<p>Free State won their second match of the season.</p>
<p>Earlier Kosie Venter scored a half-century as Free State</p>
<p>showed the application Transvaal were to lack in taking their</p>
<p>second innings to 246 before being bowled out.</p>
